<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Osorkon II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 872–837 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Osorkon II was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> of the Libyan Twenty-second Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanis">Tanis</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bubastis">Bubastis</a>. He endowed temples lavishly and rebuilt the temple of Bastet at Bubastis with a great festival hall. He placed royal sons in regional commands, which turned the kingdom into a network of family fiefs.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/osorkon-ii.jpg" alt="Osorkon II" width="320" height="434" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Egypte_louvre_066.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
